    "id": "train-963",
    "question": "Oleg is an event organizer. He is organizing an event with 80 guests where 40 of them are men, half the number of men are women, and the rest are children. If he added 10 children to the guest list, how many children will there be at the event?",
    "gold": "30",
    "answer": "There are 40/2= <<40/2=20>>20 women at the event.\nHence, there are a total of 40 + 20 = <<40+20=60>>60 men and women at the event.\nSo, the total number of children at the event is 80 - 60 = <<80-60=20>>20.\nAfter Oleg added 10 children to the guest list, there are a total of 20 + 10 = <<20+10=30>>30 children.\n#### 30"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the number of children at the event, we start by analyzing the given information step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the number of men and women:**\n   - The total number of guests is 80.\n   - The number of men is 40.\n   - The number of women is half the number of men, which is \\( \\frac{40}{2} = 20 \\).\n\n2. **Calculate the number of children:**\n   - The total number of guests is the sum of the number of men, women, and children.\n   - Let \\( C \\) be the number of children. Then, we have the equation:\n     \\[\n     40 + 20 + C = 80\n     \\]\n   - Simplify the equation to find \\( C \\):\n     \\[\n     60 + C = 80\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     C = 80 - 60\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     C = 20\n     \\]\n   - So, there are 20 children initially.\n\n3. **Determine the new number of children after adding 10 more:**\n   - If Oleg adds 10 more children to the guest list, the new number of children will be:\n     \\[\n     20 + 10 = 30\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of children at the event after adding 10 more is \\(\\boxed{30}\\).",
